CP 5.6 Priority 1 — full-GPU-path cross-context exposure: verify + fix
======================================================================
Harness: f1_p1_verify.cpp  (Mistral-7B L0 q_proj [4096,4096], M=1)
Caller context: a RAW driver-API green-derived CUcontext (cuGreenCtxCreate,
  NOT cipher_rt_green_ctx_ensure) — so the library's g_green_sm_count stays
  0 and dispatch is forced down the full-GPU / PrimaryCtxGuard branch, while
  the caller still runs on a non-primary context.
Per iter: memset(C,0) on caller ctx ; dispatch ; cuMemcpyDtoH(C) on caller
  ctx — NO cross-context synchronisation.
degenerate gate: nan|inf | cos<0.85 | rel>0.35   (correct = rel~0.140)

----- BASELINE: dc804eb3 (libcipher_rt.so.pre_cp56), pre-fix -----
[ctx] raw green-derived caller ctx created (!= primary)
[ctx] cipher_rt_green_ctx_sm_count() = 0  -> dispatch takes FULL-GPU path
    iter 0    nan=0 inf=0 zeros=0    rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905   ok
    iter 1..99  nan=0 inf=0 zeros=4096 rel=1.0000 cos=0.0000  <<< DEGENERATE
    control (after primary-context drain): rel=0.1400 cos=0.9905  ok
    degenerate iters: 99 / 100
    RESULT: BROKE — full-GPU-path cross-context race reproduced

  => Confirms the Priority 1 exposure: dc804eb3's STEP 2 fix only scoped the
     guard out for the LIBRARY's green ctx. The full-GPU path still wraps the
     GEMM in PrimaryCtxGuard unconditionally; any caller on a non-primary
