----- REGRESSION: full-GPU + caller-on-primary on a7ac8e97 -----
    (f1_p1_regr_primary = Step 1 harness repointed at the fixed build; the
     common path — no green ctx, caller already on primary. The fix records
     the event + issues a same-stream self-wait on the primary NULL stream.)
    single-GEMM: nan=0 inf=0 rel_err=0.140021 cos=0.990536
    RESULT: PASS — self-wait is harmless; no crash/hang/error/numeric change

======================================================================
THE FIX (cipher_rt_marlin_engine.cpp, cipher_rt_marlin_engine_dispatch,
no-green / full-GPU branch):

  After marlin_gemm_launch, while the PrimaryCtxGuard still holds the
  primary context current, record a CU_EVENT_DISABLE_TIMING completion
  event on the GEMM's launch stream. After the guard destructor restores
  the caller's context, cuStreamWaitEvent(stream, event) enqueues a wait on
  the caller's stream (a NULL stream resolves to the caller context's
  default stream — the F1 race case). cuStreamWaitEvent honours an event
  recorded in a different context, so this is the cross-context ordering
  primitive. Non-blocking: the host does not stall; the producer/consumer
  dependency is enforced GPU-side. Per-call event create/record/destroy;
  an event pool is a Phase-5 perf concern, not correctness.

  Added to the engine's g_api: cuEventCreate / cuEventRecord /
  cuEventDestroy_v2 / cuStreamWaitEvent (4 dlsyms). Green path UNCHANGED.

ANCHOR ROTATION: dc804eb3 -> a7ac8e97
